# 9. M41.05.07 — AUTOMATIC WAITLIST PLACEMENT

When a program reaches capacity, eligible applicants must be handled according to the program's configured waitlist policy.

Where waitlisting is enabled:

- Create a durable waitlist record.
- Assign an authoritative queue position.
- Preserve application timestamp.
- Record waitlist entry.
- Notify the member.
- Make waitlist status visible to the member.

Do not expose other applicants' identities.

### Queue ordering

Use the existing authorized waitlist policy.

If no policy exists, implement deterministic first-in-first-out ordering, with a stable secondary identifier to resolve equal timestamps.

Document the policy.

Do not silently reorder the waitlist.

